<title>TURKEY: Turk central bank reserves down $74 mln last week.</title>
<headline>Turk central bank reserves down $74 mln last week.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Turkish central bank said on Thursday its foreign currency reserves fell $74 million last week to $15.696 billion on August 23.</p>
<p>Figures in billion dollars:</p>
<p>				     Aug 23	 Aug 16	end-1995</p>
<p> Forex reserves		 15.696	  15.770	   12.391</p>
<p> Gold reserves		   1.383	   1.383	    1.383</p>
<p> Total reserves		 17.079	  17.153	   13.774</p>
<p>Gross international reserves, including gold and commercial bank holdings, rose $297 million to $26.776 billion in the week ending August 9, the bank said.</p>
<p>It said Turkey had serviced $6.010 billion of state foreign debt in the period of January 1-August 28, including $4.770 billion repaid by the treasury.</p>
<p>--Ankara Newsroom, 90-312-4462940</p>
</text>
